<title>SOUTH KOREA: Creditors to give rescue loans to S.Korea Dainong.</title>
<headline>Creditors to give rescue loans to S.Korea Dainong.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Creditor banks to South Korea's Dainong Group have decided to supply a total of 15.9 billion won in emergency loans to its two major affiliates, a SEOULBANK official said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The official at the primary lending bank said creditors have agreed to grant 5.7 billion won in loans to Dainong Corp and 10.2 billion won to Midopa Department Store .</p>
<p>Earlier, a SEOULBANK official said the two companies had requested 78 billion won in total. But a statement from Dainong later said they had requested 86.2 billion won.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
